# ACL file — topic-level access control.
# Defense in depth: even on an isolated AP network, least privilege matters.
#
# User patterns:
#   worker  - cloud pipeline. Reads everything; publishes alerts + DLQ.
#   esp32-* - devices. Publish their own telemetry; subscribe to own cmd/alert.
#   demo    - dashboards and debugging. Read-only on everything.

# ------- Worker (consumer + publisher) -------
user worker
topic read  iotpdm/#
topic write iotpdm/+/+/+/alert
topic write iotpdm/+/+/+/dlq
topic write iotpdm/+/+/+/cmd
topic read  $SYS/#

# ------- Per-device ACLs (pattern uses %u substitution = client username) -------
# NOTE: ESP32 client_id MUST equal username (we set DEVICE_ID = esp32-a17 = username).
pattern write iotpdm/+/+/%u/features
pattern write iotpdm/+/+/%u/burst
pattern write iotpdm/+/+/%u/status
pattern write iotpdm/+/+/%u/dlq
pattern read  iotpdm/+/+/%u/cmd
pattern read  iotpdm/+/+/%u/alert

# ------- Read-only demo user for dashboards -------
user demo
topic read iotpdm/#
topic read $SYS/#
